{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PwdVuAaMMa7ovDmnncz15g","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the context filesystem, the answer is **NO** — the dedicated configuration to cap the maximum size of headers was **not** kept in the final design.\\\\n\\\\nHere's the evolution from the discussion file:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Initial Proposal** (line 17): The KIP proposed \\\\\\\"Configuration to cap the size of headers written into state\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n2. **Removal in Window 8** (line 67): In the major design update addressing community feedback, Alieh Saeedi stated:\\\\n   > \\\\\\\"**Header Size and Format**: Removed the two-byte header size and its configuration property. Since varints are used for header count and individual key/value sizes, a global \\\\\\\"headers size\\\\\\\" field is redundant.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n3. **Later Re-introduction of Header Size Field** (line 111): A varint `header_size` field was later introduced in Window 17 updates, but this was specifically for **lazy deserialization when scanning large ranges**, not for capping header sizes.\\\\n\\\\nThe dedicated configuration property for capping header sizes was eliminated because the varint encoding of header counts and individual key/value sizes already provides sufficient size information, making a separate configuration redundant.\\\\n\\\\n**Source:** `/store/discussions/kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md` (lines 67 and 111)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"issues/kafka-20056-streams-record-headers-state-stores.md\\\",\\\"discussions/kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":18.97,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":77822,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":10660,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0370102,\\\"input_tokens\\\":58,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1570}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f9f1885b-4784-4f66-8055-414fc1a03cce","uuid":"350ca9a5-ce4f-4a41-8bfb-a68d380c47fd","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:43:58.472Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the context filesystem, the answer is **NO** — the dedicated configuration to cap the maximum size of headers was **not** kept in the final design.\\\\n\\\\nHere's the evolution from the discussion file:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Initial Proposal** (line 17): The KIP proposed \\\\\\\"Configuration to cap the size of headers written into state\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n2. **Removal in Window 8** (line 67): In the major design update addressing community feedback, Alieh Saeedi stated:\\\\n   > \\\\\\\"**Header Size and Format**: Removed the two-byte header size and its configuration property. Since varints are used for header count and individual key/value sizes, a global \\\\\\\"headers size\\\\\\\" field is redundant.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n3. **Later Re-introduction of Header Size Field** (line 111): A varint `header_size` field was later introduced in Window 17 updates, but this was specifically for **lazy deserialization when scanning large ranges**, not for capping header sizes.\\\\n\\\\nThe dedicated configuration property for capping header sizes was eliminated because the varint encoding of header counts and individual key/value sizes already provides sufficient size information, making a separate configuration redundant.\\\\n\\\\n**Source:** `/store/discussions/kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md` (lines 67 and 111)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"issues/kafka-20056-streams-record-headers-state-stores.md\\\",\\\"discussions/kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":18.97,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":77822,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":10660,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0370102,\\\"input_tokens\\\":58,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1570}}\"}","_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"answer\":\"Based on the context filesystem, the answer is **NO** — the dedicated configuration to cap the maximum size of headers was **not** kept in the final design.\\n\\nHere's the evolution from the discussion file:\\n\\n1. **Initial Proposal** (line 17): The KIP proposed \\\"Configuration to cap the size of headers written into state\\\"\\n\\n2. **Removal in Window 8** (line 67): In the major design update addressing community feedback, Alieh Saeedi stated:\\n   > \\\"**Header Size and Format**: Removed the two-byte header size and its configuration property. Since varints are used for header count and individual key/value sizes, a global \\\"headers size\\\" field is redundant.\\\"\\n\\n3. **Later Re-introduction of Header Size Field** (line 111): A varint `header_size` field was later introduced in Window 17 updates, but this was specifically for **lazy deserialization when scanning large ranges**, not for capping header sizes.\\n\\nThe dedicated configuration property for capping header sizes was eliminated because the varint encoding of header counts and individual key/value sizes already provides sufficient size information, making a separate configuration redundant.\\n\\n**Source:** `/store/discussions/kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md` (lines 67 and 111)\",\"error\":null,\"files\":[\"store\",\"issues/kafka-20056-streams-record-headers-state-stores.md\",\"discussions/kip-1271-record-headers-state-stores.md\"],\"seconds\":18.97,\"truncated\":false,\"turns\":2,\"usage\":{\"cache_read_tokens\":77822,\"cache_write_tokens\":10660,\"cost_usd\":0.0370102,\"input_tokens\":58,\"output_tokens\":1570}}"}}}
